From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:38:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] settings: Kiln OS's web interface, Fluidd or Mainsail, on
 System

Settings > System > Web interface picks what opens at the printer's
address in a browser, through Moonraker's kiln_os component: the row
shows where machine.kiln_os.info lists the webui feature, lists only the
interfaces machine.kiln_os.get_webui says the printer has and shows the
choice. A pick sends machine.kiln_os.post_webui with the control greyed
until Kiln answers, then a toast says the new one and to reload the
printer's page in the browser. While the mainsail-kiln plugin serves both
(plugin in the GET, or a plugin_manages_webui refusal) the row is greyed,
"Managed by the mainsail-kiln plugin"; any other refusal shows Kiln's
message and puts the choice back. Picking the choice again sends it when
the GET says another one is served (served), which puts them in line;
only the choice that is also served sends nothing. Asked at every
connect and each time the System page opens; behind Settings > Advanced
settings; on the AD5X build only.

setting_dropdown_row takes bind_options for the list. English, English
(UK, empty) and Russian strings.
